title: "Why Pay Anyone? The Economics of Cheap Intelligence"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Ansari
    given-names: Talha
    affiliation: "BS-MS Economics, Indian Institute of Technology Roorkee"
date-released: 2026-11-25
url: "https://why-pay-anyone.vercel.app"
repository-code: "https://github.com/amsorrytola/why-pay-anyone"
abstract: >-
  An economics study of what happens to jobs, wages, prices and market power when AI makes
  intelligence cheap: public data on the price, use and adoption of AI and the structure of its market,
  a task-based labour model, growth and demand models, and an India lens built on PLFS 2025 microdata.
  Lab Based Project (HSC-400), industry track with Hello Agentic.
keywords:
  - artificial intelligence
  - labour economics
  - task-based model
  - labour share
  - market concentration
  - India
